<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Synthetic Document</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif; }
        .logo-uiw { font-size: 150px; line-height: 1; }
        .header-section { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; }
        .left-column { width: 50%; }
        .right-column { width: 50%; }
        .text-block { margin-bottom: 20px; line-height: 1.6; }
        .list-item { margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .footer-text { font-size: 10px; text-align: center; margin-top: 50px; }
        .section-title { font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .sub-heading { font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .grid-2x2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 20px; }
        .image-container { text-align: center; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <div class="header-section">
        <div class="left-column">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <img src="placeholder_image_1.jpg" alt="Campus View" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="right-column" style="text-align: right;">
            <div class="logo-uiw">UIW</div>
            <div style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: -20px;">MILITARY AND VETERAN CENTER</div>
            <div style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold;">VETERAN'S PROGRAMS GUIDE</div>
            <div style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">2021-2022</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 32px; font-weight: bold;">Military and Veteran Center</h2>
        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
            <span data-field="address_line_1">{{ address_line_1 }}</span><br>
            <span data-field="city_state_zip">{{ city_state_zip }}</span>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <p>Student Engagement Center</p>
            <p>Level 3, Room 3021</p>
            <p>Email: <span data-field="email">{{ email }}</span></p>
            <p>Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span></p>
            <p>Fax: <span data-field="fax_number">{{ fax_number }}</span></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="position: absolute; bottom: 50px; left: 50px; text-align: center;">
        <img src="placeholder_logo_uiw.png" alt="UIW Logo" style="width: 100px;">
        <div style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px;">
            UNIVERSITY OF THE<br>
            INCARNATE WORD<br>
            MILITARY & VETERAN CENTER
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <div class="text-block">
                    <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">Welcome to the Nest</h2>
                    <p>Congratulations on your acceptance to UIW! We are excited to help you navigate your journey to obtaining a college degree. The UIW Military and Veteran Center has a dedicated staff who is here to assist you with any questions you may have regarding the upcoming <span data-field="academic_year">{{ academic_year }}</span> academic year. It has been a difficult and challenging time during the COVID-19 pandemic, but UIW has taken precautions to ensure the health and safety of our staff and students. The start of this new year will see more in-person classes, and we are excited to welcome everyone to our beautiful campus.</p>
                    <p>UIW is proud to serve our nation's veterans, and we strive to be the best college experience for those who have served our great nation. In doing so, we offer the following:</p>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_1">{{ benefit_1 }}</span></li>
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_2">{{ benefit_2 }}</span></li>
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_3">{{ benefit_3 }}</span></li>
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_4">{{ benefit_4 }}</span></li>
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_5">{{ benefit_5 }}</span></li>
                        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefit_6">{{ benefit_6 }}</span></li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The University of the Incarnate Word's president, Dr. <span data-field="president_last_name">{{ president_last_name }}</span>, has laid out eight strategic priorities. One of the priorities is to be the premier provider for those who have served their country. We here in the Military and Veteran Center are doing everything we can live out that mission. If you need any assistance during your time at UIW, our office is here to provide you with any help we can.</p>
                    <p>Once again, congratulations on your acceptance to the University and welcome to the Nest, Cardinal!</p>
                    <p>- Your Military and Veteran Center Office</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: center;">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 32px; font-weight: bold; color: #c00;">Veteran Tribute Stole</h2>
                <img src="placeholder_image_2.jpg" alt="Veteran Tribute Stole" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-top: 20px;">
                <div class="text-block" style="margin-top: 20px;">
                    <p>If you are a graduating UIW student veteran, you can request a veteran tribute stole.</p>
                    <p>A veteran stole is provided for free to all veterans upon request by the UIW Military and Veteran Center. Students can either request their stole to be mailed or to pick it up in person.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <div style="text-align: left;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">Purepost Profile</h2>
                <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-top: 15px;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Cardinal</h3>
                    <p>Purepost allows you to get a head start with understanding how your experience translates to private sector skills and experience.</p>
                    <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
                        <p><strong>The Benefits</strong></p>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li class="list-item">UIW career professionals have immediate access to your profile to begin providing feedback and guidance on creating a resume.</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Free for all students.</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Takes less than 30 minutes to complete.</li>
                            <li class="list-item">UIW career professionals may share profiles with partners to maximize your future opportunities.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">
                        <a href="#" style="text-decoration: none; color: blue;">Go to https://www.purepost.co/uiw</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: left;">
            <div style="text-align: left;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">Veterans Integration to Academic Leadership</h2>
                <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
                    <p><strong>What is VITAL?</strong></p>
                    <p>The VITAL initiative is a partnership between the VA Healthcare System and local colleges and universities to support student veterans. VITAL helps students navigate the healthcare services and promotes a positive relationship between veterans and the entire learning community through campus and community education and training.</p>
                    <p><strong>How the VITAL Program Can Benefit Student Veterans:</strong></p>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">Provide education on various VA benefits and services Veterans are entitled to as well as assist with enrollment into VA healthcare.</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Assist veterans in accessing and navigating available VA resources as well as community and on campus services.</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Provide brief counseling services to eligible Student Veterans.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>To receive ongoing VITAL services eligible Student Veterans must:</p>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">Meet Veterans Health Administration criteria for healthcare services.</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Be enrolled in the VA healthcare system.</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Not be eligible for VA healthcare the VITAL coordinator will assist veterans in accessing on campus and community services.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If a Veteran is not yet enrolled in VA services or needs help understanding eligibility requirements for VA healthcare the VITAL Coordinator can assist them.</p>
                    <p><strong>Mission Statement:</strong></p>
                    <p>The mission of VITAL is to provide world-class healthcare to the overall quality of life for Veterans, while supporting their successful integration into college and university campuses. VITAL achieves this through seamless access to VA healthcare services and on-campus resources.</p>
                    <p>If you have any questions or wish to learn more about VITAL services contact:</p>
                    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">
                        <p>Colleen Ward, LCSW<br>VITAL Program Coordinator<br>(726) 300-2885</p>
                        <img src="placeholder_vital_logo.png" alt="VITAL Logo" style="width: 150px; margin-top: 10px;">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <img src="placeholder_image_3.jpg" alt="Army ROTC" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
                    <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">ARMY ROTC TWO YEAR PROGRAM</h2>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold;">FOR GRADUATE STUDENTS</h3>
                    <p>UIW ROTC is accepting qualified students with at least 60 credit hours to enroll in Army ROTC and take the course as a junior and senior. Or, if you are pursuing a master's degree, you may also qualify! All applicants may be eligible for a full scholarship plus room and board.</p>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 25px;">Requirements:</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">Be a U.S. citizen</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Must have 60 or more college hours towards your degree, or be working towards a master's program</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Must be enrolled at the University of the Incarnate Word</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Must obtain your degree and commission as an officer by your 30th birthday</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Meet Physical and Medical standards</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Agree to accept a commission and serve in the Army on active duty, reserve component or National Guard</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Must have prior service or more than three years of ROTC experience – if not, need to attend Basic Camp</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 25px;">Army ROTC Basic Camp:</h3>
                    <p>Must be completed before enrolling in junior/senior years as an Army ROTC Cadet</p>
                    <p>Four weeks of leadership training and team building at Fort Knox, Kentucky</p>
                    <p>Free travel and lodging</p>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 25px;">Potential Scholarships:</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">Full tuition and fees!</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Monthly stipend and book allowance!</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Potential University Incentives – free room and board</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Worldwide travel and adventures</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 25px;">Commitment:</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li class="list-item">An eight-year service commitment to the Army as an Army Officer.</li>
                        <li class="list-item">Choose to serve in one of twenty-four branches in the Army! Including Medical Corps, Nurse Corps and more!</li>
                        <li class="list-item">You can either serve all eight years in the reserve components of the Army, or four years active and four years reserve.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="margin-top: 30px;">Call/email the UIW ROTC Enrollment Officer for more information:</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold;">210-638-1784 / ROTC@UIWTX.EDU</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: center;">
            <div class="grid-2x2">
                <div class="image-container">
                    <img src="placeholder_image_4.jpg" alt="Student Veterans" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                    <p style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 10px;">Did you know as a student veteran you may qualify for free meals?</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px;">Meals for Vets is a program that provides student veterans who have low income with free daily meals.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="image-container">
                    <img src="placeholder_image_5.jpg" alt="Meals for Vets" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; margin-top: 10px;">
                        <p><strong>To qualify:</strong></p>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li class="list-item">Must have served at least 180 days federal active duty</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Provide proof of service (such as DD-214)</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Provide proof of all household income and benefits</li>
                            <li class="list-item">Meet low income qualifications</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p><strong>To learn more and apply, call:</strong></p>
                        <p>Meals for Vets<br>830-992-3375</p>
                        <p><strong>Or apply online:</strong></p>
                        <p><a href="#">mealsforvets.org/help</a></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 50%;">
            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <img src="placeholder_image_6.jpg" alt="SVA Chapter" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
                    <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">SVA Chapter</h2>
                    <div style="border: 2px solid red; padding: 20px; margin-top: 20px;">
                        <p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">IN 2009, THE STUDENT VETERANS AT THE UNIVERSITY OF THE INCARNATE WORD ESTABLISHED A <span data-field="chapter_name">{{ chapter_name }}</span>.</p>
                        <p>THE MISSION OF UIW'S CHAPTER OF THE STUDENT VETERANS OF AMERICA IS TO EXPEDITE, FACILITATE AND REINFORCE THE SUCCESSFUL TRANSITION FOR U.S. MILITARY VETERANS AND THEIR FAMILIES TO UNIVERSITY LIFE, WHILE FOSTERING A LASTING BOND OF FRIENDSHIP WITH VETERANS OF ALL ARMED FORCES AND MENTORING THE NEXT GENERATION OF MILITARY AND CIVILIAN LEADERSHIP.</p>
                        <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">
                            <img src="placeholder_sva_logo.png" alt="SVA Logo" style="width: 150px;">
                            <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px;">SCAN TO LEARN MORE ON HOW TO BECOME A CARDINAL WARRIOR...</p>
                            <img src="placeholder_qr_code.png" alt="QR Code" style="width: 100px; margin-top: 10px;">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: left;">
            <div style="text-align: left;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold;">Peer Advisors for Veteran Education (PAVE)</h2>
                <p>PAVE is a peer support program that connects incoming student veterans with student veterans already on campus to help them navigate the transition to university life. PAVE helps the student to appropriate resources on or off campus, and provide ongoing support toward academic and personal goals. UIW is one of three colleges in Texas, and one of 47 throughout the country, to have been awarded the PAVE program.</p>
                <p><strong>The goals of the program are to:</strong></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li class="list-item">Ease the transition from military to university life.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Improve student veterans' sense of connectedness to the university.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Help student veterans navigate the resources available to them.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Identify mental health issues and other concerns in a timely fashion and connect student veterans with appropriate resources.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Improve student veteran academic performance.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Increase student veteran retention rates.</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Advisors sharing their own experiences of the university.</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Activities:</strong></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li class="list-item">Meet and greets and socials to connect with other student veterans.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Networking.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Career readiness.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Special guest speakers.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>For more information about PAVE:</p>
                <p>Visit our website: <span data-field="pave_website">{{ pave_website }}</span></p>
                <p>E-mail us: <span data-field="pave_email">{{ pave_email }}</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>